  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q23-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "23",
    "prompt": "If 2 kilograms of bananas and 3 kilograms of apples cost $\\$19$ and 5 kilograms of bananas and 4 kilograms of apples cost $\\$30$, then find the cost per kilogram of bananas and apples.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Bananas cost $\\$2$ per kilogram and apples cost $\\$5$ per kilogram.",
      "worked": "Let $b$ and $a$ be the prices in dollars per kilogram of bananas and apples respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2b+3a&=19 &&(1)\\\\5b+4a&=30 &&(2)\\\\10b+15a&=95 &&5\\times(1)\\\\10b+8a&=60 &&2\\times(2)\\\\7a&=35 &&\\text{subtract}\\\\a&=5\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute $a=5$ into (1):\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2b+3(5)&=19\\\\2b&=4\\\\b&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nBananas cost $\\$2$ per kilogram and apples cost $\\$5$ per kilogram.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 108
  },
